	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Desolace is a grey waste in the west of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, set between the peaks of {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon{/link} to the north and the forests of {link:feralas}Feralas{/link} to the south. Its earth is ash and bone. Its trees are dead, its rivers are few, and its wind carries dust from one horizon to the other. The bones of great beasts lie heaped in its heart, the ruins of an older people stand broken on its hills, and the sea beats on a coast where the {link:naga}naga{/link} hunt. It is a land where many things come to die, and where many more come to kill.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how Desolace became so barren, nor what it was called before it bore that name. Its ruins speak of a time when the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} dwelt here. Their towns stood on the northern hills and along the western shore, and some of their halls now lie beneath the waves near {link:ranazjar-isle}Ranazjar Isle{/link}. The elves left long ago. Those who remain say that the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} took the land after them, and the centaur themselves claim it by right of birth. Their tales say that their race was born in this place, from the union of Zaetar, a son of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}, and Theradras, a princess of the elemental earth, and that the first of their kind slew their own father. His tomb lies in the caverns of {red:maraudon}Maraudon{/red} in the west of Desolace, and the centaur hold it holy.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Desolace is at war with itself. Four great clans of {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} fight over its dry plains: the {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar{/link} in the east, the Magram in the south-east, the Gelkis in the south-west and the Maraudine, who guard the tomb of Maraudon from the {link:valley-of-spears}Valley of Spears{/link}. The clans hate one another more than they hate outsiders, and both the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} have learned to use that hatred. Each has sent envoys to buy the friendship of one clan with the blood of another.

The centaur are not the only danger. The orcs of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} hold {link:thunder-axe-fortress}Thunder Axe Fortress{/link} in the north, and at {link:mannoroc-coven}Mannoroc Coven{/link} in the south demons of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} pass freely into the world through portals the cultists keep open. The {link:satyrs}satyr{/link} of the Hatefury haunt the ruins of {link:sargeron}Sargeron{/link}. The Slitherblade {link:naga}naga{/link} hold the reefs of the western coast. In the south-east, the ghosts of dead centaur walk a valley of bones, and some say that other dead walk there too.

Against all this stand a handful of camps. The Alliance holds {link:nijels-point}Nijel's Point{/link}, high in the northern mountains. The Horde keeps {link:ghost-walker-post}Ghost Walker Post{/link} above the {link:kodo-graveyard}Kodo Graveyard{/link}, and the trolls of {link:shadowprey-village}Shadowprey Village{/link} fish the western shore. Goblin traders run a kodo caravan through the middle of the land and buy bones by the cartload. Druids of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} have come to ask for help against the corruption in Maraudon, and a centaur outcast wanders the south, dreaming of a single tribe.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}.{/b} The {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar{/link}, Magram, Gelkis and Maraudine clans, each ruled by its own khan.
• {b}The {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link}.{/b} Orc cultists who serve demons from {link:thunder-axe-fortress}Thunder Axe Fortress{/link} and {link:mannoroc-coven}Mannoroc Coven{/link}.
• {b}The demons.{/b} Nether maidens, doomwarders, mage hunters and felhounds that come through the portals of the coven.
• {b}The {link:satyrs}satyr{/link}.{/b} The Hatefury, who dwell in the ruins of {link:sargeron}Sargeron{/link}.
• {b}The {link:naga}naga{/link}.{/b} The Slitherblade, who hold the reefs of the western coast and {link:ranazjar-isle}Ranazjar Isle{/link}.
• {b}The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.{/b} Soldiers, {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} agents, dwarven treasure-seekers and a lone brother of the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} at {link:nijels-point}Nijel's Point{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link} and {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:ghost-walker-post}Ghost Walker Post{/link}, and the trolls and tauren of {link:shadowprey-village}Shadowprey Village{/link}.
• {b}The goblins.{/b} Traders in kodo, kodo bones and anything else that sells.
• {b}The beasts.{/b} Kodo old and dying, scorpashi, thunder lizards, and the great sea giants of the coast.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Elven Age.{/b} Night elves once built towns on these hills and shores. No chronicle records when they came or why they left.
• {b}The Birth of the Centaur.{/b} The {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} tell that their race began here with Zaetar and Theradras, and that Zaetar was slain by his own children.
• {b}The Clan Wars.{/b} For as long as anyone remembers, the centaur clans have fought one another for the land.
• {b}The Coming of the Blade.{/b} After the {link:horde}Horde{/link} came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} claimed {link:thunder-axe-fortress}Thunder Axe Fortress{/link} and opened the way for demons at {link:mannoroc-coven}Mannoroc Coven{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the Horde each send agents to set the clans against each other and to root out the cultists before the demons grow too strong.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Waste",
			text = [=[• The kodo of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} are said to walk to Desolace when their time comes, to lie down among the bones of their ancestors.
• The Gelkis believe that Theradras protects them, and they keep crystals they call her tears. The Magram laugh at them.
• A {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} at {link:nijels-point}Nijel's Point{/link} admits that he has no idea who Nijel was.
• The ghosts of the {link:valley-of-bones}Valley of Bones{/link} are Magram dead. A goblin once tried to sell their essence back to the living Magram.]=],
		},
	},
})

